r before his failing hands give out.","goal":"Forge a new cable strong enough to replace the oldest span, the Weaver's Reach.","flaw":"Clings rigidly to traditional methods and scorns innovation.","internal_conflict":"He is ashamed that his tremor has made his latest braids imperfect.","external_conflict":"Cloudstone stocks are being bought up by the Cartel, starving his forge.","arc":"Bram learns to accept new techniques and to teach rather than hoard his mastery, completing his legacy through Isolde's designs.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","proud","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Master Braiding","description":"Weaves cloudstone strands into cables of exceptional strength.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_halewind","name":"Corvin Halewind","description":"A charismatic young factor of the Drift Cartel at Mistral Docks, with silver-threaded coats and a quick, disarming smile. Born poor on the docks, he climbed by shrewd dealing and now oversees skybridge tolls.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure wealth and status so he never returns to dockside poverty.","goal":"Raise tolls and monopolize skybridge access, making the Cartel indispensable.","flaw":"Equates worth with profit and cannot value what cannot be sold.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the toll revenue is not funding repairs and that his success rests on neglected bridges.","external_conflict":"Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his levies, and the Toll War threatens his standing with Cartel princes.","arc":"Corvin's schemes expose the real cost of neglected bridges, and he is forced to choose between his fortune and the realm's survival, ending in uneasy redemption.","personality_traits":["charming","ambitious","calculating","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates and persuades with unsettling ease.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_tillerbrook","name":"Wren 