{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","description":"A twenty-year-old senior cartography student at Silverspine Academy, Isolde is lanky and ink-stained, with wind-tangled auburn hair and a satchel of brass drafting tools. Raised by a Bridge Warden mother who vanished while inspecting a failing span, she learned to read the drift of the isles as other children learn to read letters.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To honor her missing mother by ensuring no family is ever stranded by a falling skybridge.","goal":"Chart and repair the failing skybridges before the isles drift beyond reach of one another.","flaw":"Trusts her maps over people, dismissing advice that contradicts her measurements.","internal_conflict":"She fears that her mother's disappearance was caused by a mistake she is destined to repeat.","external_conflict":"Rising Cartel tolls and the Wardens' dwindling resources make every repair a political battle.","arc":"Isolde moves from solitary perfectionism to leading a coalition of forgers, farmers and merchants, learning that the realm is held together by trust as much as cloudstone.","personality_traits":["curious","stubborn","meticulous","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Reading","description":"Predicts how isles will shift by interpreting wind currents and bridge tension.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cloudstone Surveying","description":"Detects hairline fractures in skybridge cables by touch and sound.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_cinderlock","name":"Bram Cinderlock","description":"A broad-shouldered master braider of Emberroost with singed eyebrows and forearms scarred by cable-burn. He has braided cloudstone for thirty years and speaks in slow, gravelly sentences.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To pass his craft to a worthy successor before his failing hands give out.","goal":"Forge a new cable strong enough to replace the oldest span, the Weaver's Reach.","flaw":"Clings rigidly to traditional methods and scorns innovation.","internal_conflict":"He is ashamed that his tremor has made his latest braids imperfect.","external_conflict":"Cloudstone stocks are being bought up by the Cartel, starving his forge.","arc":"Bram learns to accept new techniques and to teach rather than hoard his mastery, completing his legacy through Isolde's designs.","personality_traits":["gruff","loyal","proud","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Master Braiding","description":"Weaves cloudstone strands into cables of exceptional strength.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_halewind","name":"Corvin Halewind","description":"A charismatic young factor of the Drift Cartel at Mistral Docks, with silver-threaded coats and a quick, disarming smile. Born poor on the docks, he climbed by shrewd dealing and now oversees skybridge tolls.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure wealth and status so he never returns to dockside poverty.","goal":"Raise tolls and monopolize skybridge access, making the Cartel indispensable.","flaw":"Equates worth with profit and cannot value what cannot be sold.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the toll revenue is not funding repairs and that his success rests on neglected bridges.","external_conflict":"Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his levies, and the Toll War threatens his standing with Cartel princes.","arc":"Corvin's schemes expose the real cost of neglected bridges, and he is forced to choose between his fortune and the realm's survival, ending in uneasy redemption.","personality_traits":["charming","ambitious","calculating","insecure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates and persuades with unsettling ease.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_wren_tillerbrook","name":"Wren Tillerbrook","description":"A sixteen-year-old miller's apprentice from The Hollow, freckled and sunburnt, who has never left her isle. She tinkers with windmill gearing and dreams of seeing the other isles.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To see the wider realm and prove the Hollow's quiet labour matters.","goal":"Secure safe passage for her isle's grain without surrendering to the Cartel levy.","flaw":"Impulsive, she acts before considering consequences.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between loyalty to her family's quiet traditions and her hunger for adventure.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy threatens her family's livelihood and wind-debt keeps them tied to the Cartel.","arc":"Wren grows from reckless eagerness into a thoughtful advocate for the Hollow, using her mechanical skill to help Isolde's repairs.","personality_traits":["cheerful","bold","inventive","restless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Tinkering","description":"Improvises gears and wind-driven mechanisms from scrap.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_marek_osse","name":"Marek Osse","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden captain stationed at Silverspine, gaunt and silver-haired, who served alongside Isolde's mother. He carries her last survey log.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To atone for failing to save Isolde's mother.","goal":"Keep the Wardens funded and the bridges standing despite Cartel pressure.","flaw":"Withholds painful truths, believing he protects others.","internal_conflict":"He hides that he ordered the inspection that led to Isolde's mother's disappearance.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls undermine the Wardens' budget and authority.","arc":"Marek confesses his secret, earning Isolde's painful forgiveness, and makes a final stand to protect the network.","personality_traits":["stoic","guilt-ridden","dutiful","protective"],"abilities":[{"name":"Warden Tactics","description":"Coordinates emergency bridge repairs under dangerous conditions.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_mentored_by_marek","source_character_id":"chr_marek_osse","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Marek Osse acts as a guarded mentor to Isolde Vane, guiding her while concealing his role in her mother's disappearance."},{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewind","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane opposes Corvin Halewind's rising tolls, which block the repairs she believes can save the realm."},{"id":"rel_corvin_isolde_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewind","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Halewind sees Isolde Vane's repairs as a threat to Cartel toll revenue and works to obstruct her."},{"id":"rel_bram_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_bram_cinderlock","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Bram Cinderlock teaches Isolde Vane the craft of cloudstone braiding, though he resists her innovative designs."},{"id":"rel_wren_isolde_ally","source_character_id":"chr_wren_tillerbrook","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Wren Tillerbrook joins Isolde Vane's mission, offering mechanical ingenuity in exchange for passage beyond the Hollow."},{"id":"rel_wren_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_wren_tillerbrook","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_halewind","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Wren Tillerbrook resents Corvin Halewind for enforcing the Grain Levy that threatens her family's mill."}]}
