{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vance","name":"Mara Vance","role":"protagonist","description":"A former Bridge Warden inspector turned private investigator, Mara is in her late thirties, with a weathered grey coat, cropped dark hair, and a limp from a skybridge accident she was blamed for. She works out of a cramped office above the Mistral Docks fish market, where the rain of drifting storm-fronts never quite stops.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To clear her name after being scapegoated for a bridge failure and to prove that truth can still be found in a city of liars.","goal":"Unmask the blackmailer and recover the letters that are ruining lives across the isles.","flaw":"She trusts only her own conclusions and dismisses help that doesn't fit her theory.","internal_conflict":"She craves vindication but fears that exposing the truth will expose her own old mistakes.","external_conflict":"Cartel agents and Wardens alike obstruct her inquiries while she works against the clock before the next blackmail deadline.","arc":"Mara begins as a guarded loner who tests every alibi alone. She learns to rely on allies, accepts her part in her past failure, and finishes the case choosing justice over personal vindication.","personality_traits":["cynical","observant","stubborn","dry-witted"],"abilities":[{"name":"Alibi Breaker","description":"Cross-checks wind-debt ledgers and crossing times to expose false alibis.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Bridge Lore","description":"Knows skybridge mechanics and can tell when a crossing was tampered with.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_silas_crowe","name":"Silas Crowe","role":"antagonist","description":"A soft-spoken cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers and a tidy silver beard. He charts the bridge network, which gives him knowledge of who crossed where and when, and he has quietly turned that knowledge into leverage.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To buy back his family's estate and escape the crushing wind-debt that has bound him for years.","goal":"Collect enough blackmail payments to clear his debt and vanish from the archipelago.","flaw":"He is vain about his cleverness and cannot resist taunting those hunting him.","internal_conflict":"He sees himself as a scholar of truth yet profits from twisting it into a weapon.","external_conflict":"Mara closes in while the Cartel demands a share of his profits.","arc":"Silas grows bolder as the payments roll in, then unravels when his vanity leaves clues. He ends exposed, forced to confront what his scholarship became.","personality_traits":["polite","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crossing Records","description":"Reads the shifting route charts to reconstruct anyone's movements.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Forged Alibis","description":"Fabricates convincing timelines that mislead investigators.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_fenn","name":"Tobias Fenn","role":"supporting","description":"A young dock clerk with restless eyes and a patched Cartel coat, Tobias logs every arrival at Mistral Docks. He is underpaid, anxious, and knows far more than he admits.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To protect his sick mother by keeping his job and staying out of trouble.","goal":"Survive the investigation without implicating himself or his employers.","flaw":"He lies reflexively when frightened.","internal_conflict":"He wants to help Mara but fears losing the Cartel's protection.","external_conflict":"Cartel superiors punish any clerk who talks to investigators.","arc":"Tobias evades Mara at first, then chooses to testify with his true dock logs, trading security for integrity.","personality_traits":["nervous","loyal","observant"],"abilities":[{"name":"Dock Ledger Memory","description":"Remembers arrival and departure details of vessels with surprising accuracy.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_odalys_brandt","name":"Odalys Brandt","role":"supporting","description":"A broad-shouldered Hollow Circle miller whose flour-dusted hands hide a sharp mind. She is a victim of the blackmailer and the first to hire Mara, carrying her secret as a heavy burden.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep a hidden debt deal from destroying her community's standing.","goal":"Stop the blackmail without public scandal.","flaw":"Pride keeps her from admitting the whole truth to Mara.","internal_conflict":"She values honesty but is guarding a secret that shames her.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy tightens the Cartel's grip on her, and the blackmailer keeps raising the price.","arc":"Odalys withholds details and nearly sinks the case, then confesses openly and becomes a key witness.","personality_traits":["proud","practical","warm"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community Standing","description":"Mobilizes Hollow farmers to supply shelter, information, and aid.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_hunts_silas","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vance","target_character_id":"chr_silas_crowe","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Mara Vance hunts Silas Crowe as the blackmailer, and he in turn tries to mislead her with forged alibis."},{"id":"rel_mara_pressures_tobias","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vance","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_fenn","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Mara Vance leans on dock clerk Tobias Fenn for his logs, slowly turning a frightened witness into an ally."},{"id":"rel_odalys_hires_mara","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_brandt","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vance","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Odalys Brandt hires Mara Vance to find her blackmailer, yet withholds truths that endanger the case."},{"id":"rel_silas_squeezes_odalys","source_character_id":"chr_silas_crowe","target_character_id":"chr_odalys_brandt","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Silas Crowe blackmails Odalys Brandt, raising his demands each time she pays."}]}
