[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_vell","name":"Mara Vell","role":"protagonist","description":"A weathered former skybridge surveyor in her late thirties, born on Silverspine Academy to a family of cartographers. Years ago she mapped a route into an overgrown jungle island that swallowed her entire survey crew, and she has refused to speak of it since. She has sun-darkened skin, a rope-scarred left palm, and a patched coat stitched with cloudstone thread.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To atone for the crew she lost by making sure no one else is consumed by the jungle isle.","goal":"Lead the expedition in and out of the lost city alive, then burn her old survey charts so the route is forgotten.","flaw":"Chronic self-reliance that makes her hide dangerous truths from her allies.","internal_conflict":"She wants to forget the jungle but knows she is the only one who can find the way back through it.","external_conflict":"The expedition's backers want the route preserved and sold, while the jungle itself reshapes paths behind them.","arc":"Mara begins as a reluctant guide who withholds what she knows, learns to trust the expedition with the truth about her past failure, and ends by choosing to seal the route knowingly and publicly rather than hide it.","personality_traits":["guarded","dry-witted","observant","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Pathfinding","description":"Reads wind, cable tension, and drift patterns to find safe crossings between isles and through unmapped terrain.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Cloudstone Rigging","description":"Braids and repairs cloudstone cable to build emergency crossings and climbing lines.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_drax","name":"Corvin Drax","role":"antagonist","description":"A charming, silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties who funds the expedition. He wears tailored crimson coats, rings of trade seals, and a pair of wind-goggles he never removes. He rose from dock clerk to financier through ruthless contracts.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To seize the lost city's wealth and secure a trade monopoly that makes the Cartel untouchable.","goal":"Claim the city's treasures and the route to it before the Bridge Wardens can declare it protected.","flaw":"Greed that blinds him to danger and makes him treat people as expendable collateral.","internal_conflict":"He fears that without ever-growing wealth he will be exposed as the dock clerk he once was.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves the Wardens and Hollow Circle watching him, and the jungle punishes anyone who takes from it.","arc":"Corvin starts as a gracious patron, shows his ruthlessness as the jungle strips away his comforts, and is ultimately undone by the very hoarding instinct that drives him.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract Leverage","description":"Binds people with wind-debt and carefully worded contracts so they owe him labour or goods.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","description":"A young, earnest Hollow Circle miller's son in his early twenties, hired as the expedition's porter and cook. He is lanky, freckled, and always smells faintly of grain dust. He joined to pay off a family wind-debt.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To clear his family's crushing wind-debt and keep their windmills from being seized.","goal":"Earn enough from the expedition's pay to repay the Cartel levy and wind-debt in full.","flaw":"Naive trust in authority that makes him easy for powerful people to manipulate.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be loyal to his employer yet increasingly senses Corvin is dangerous.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy threatens his family, and the jungle's dangers threaten his survival.","arc":"Tobias moves from eager obedience to doubt, then finds the courage to side with Mara against Corvin and to stand up for his community.","personality_traits":["cheerful","loyal","naive","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Hardy Provisioner","description":"Stretches meagre supplies and prepares safe food from unfamiliar plants.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_ilsa_quill","name":"Dr. Ilsa Quill","role":"supporting","description":"A brilliant, brusque Silverspine Academy scholar in her forties, leading the expedition's research. She is small, ink-stained, and carries a brass-bound journal everywhere. She has spent her career chasing rumours of the lost city.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove the lost city existed and document its history before it is looted or lost.","goal":"Record and preserve the city's inscriptions and architecture intact.","flaw":"Obsessive curiosity that makes her ignore warnings and risk others' safety.","internal_conflict":"She must choose between scholarly glory and protecting the site from exploitation.","external_conflict":"Corvin's plundering plans conflict with her preservation goals, and the jungle destroys her records.","arc":"Ilsa starts willing to overlook Corvin's motives for access, comes to see her research enabling exploitation, and ends by choosing to protect the site over her fame.","personality_traits":["brilliant","brusque","obsessive","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ancient Script Analysis","description":"Deciphers inscriptions and architectural patterns to reveal hidden mechanisms and histories.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_sable_kest","name":"Sable Kest","role":"supporting","description":"A taciturn Emberroost forge-hand in her thirties hired as the expedition's rigger and guard. She is broad-shouldered with singed eyebrows and a cloudstone-braided bracelet. She is fiercely protective of the people she works with.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep her companions alive and honour the Warden oath to protect those who cross bridges.","goal":"Ensure every member of the expedition returns home across the final skybridge.","flaw":"Rigid sense of duty that makes her slow to question orders, even bad ones.","internal_conflict":"Her oath to protect clashes with her growing suspicion that the mission itself is harming people.","external_conflict":"Corvin's orders endanger the party, and the rule against open flame limits her tools in the jungle.","arc":"Sable moves from unquestioning obedience to open defiance, realizing true duty lies with people rather than patrons.","personality_traits":["stoic","protective","disciplined","blunt"],"abilities":[{"name":"Forge-Hardened Strength","description":"Trained in heavy labour and combat with hammers and cable hooks.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_corvin_patron","source_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_drax","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Vell is bound by contract to guide Corvin Drax, who bought her debt, and she distrusts his plan to plunder the city while he presses her to reveal the route she has long concealed."},{"id":"rel_corvin_tobias_debt","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_drax","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"employer","description":"Corvin Drax exploits Tobias Wren's family wind-debt and the Cartel's grain levy to keep the young porter obedient and expendable."},{"id":"rel_ilsa_mara_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_ilsa_quill","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Dr. Ilsa Quill once taught Mara Vell at Silverspine Academy and now pushes her former student to share her jungle knowledge, straining their trust."},{"id":"rel_sable_mara_ally","source_character_id":"chr_sable_kest","target_character_id":"chr_mara_vell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sable Kest, a fellow Bridge Warden, quietly backs Mara Vell and becomes her closest ally as they protect the party from Corvin's reckless orders."},{"id":"rel_tobias_sable_protege","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_sable_kest","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tobias Wren looks up to Sable Kest, who shields him on the trail and helps him find the courage to oppose Corvin Drax."}]}
</Output>
