s, and a pair of wind-goggles he never removes. He rose from dock clerk to financier through ruthless contracts.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To seize the lost city's wealth and secure a trade monopoly that makes the Cartel untouchable.","goal":"Claim the city's treasures and the route to it before the Bridge Wardens can declare it protected.","flaw":"Greed that blinds him to danger and makes him treat people as expendable collateral.","internal_conflict":"He fears that without ever-growing wealth he will be exposed as the dock clerk he once was.","external_conflict":"The Toll War leaves the Wardens and Hollow Circle watching him, and the jungle punishes anyone who takes from it.","arc":"Corvin starts as a gracious patron, shows his ruthlessness as the jungle strips away his comforts, and is ultimately undone by the very hoarding instinct that drives him.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","impatient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Contract Leverage","description":"Binds people with wind-debt and carefully worded contracts so they owe him labour or goods.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","description":"A young, earnest Hollow Circle miller's son in his early twenties, hired as the expedition's porter and cook. He is lanky, freckled, and always smells faintly of grain dust. He joined to pay off a family wind-debt.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To clear his family's crushing wind-debt and keep their windmills from being seized.","goal":"Earn enough from the expedition's pay to repay the Cartel levy and wind-debt in full.","flaw":"Naive trust in authority that makes him easy for powerful people to manipulate.","internal_conflict":"He wants to be loyal to his employer yet increasingly senses Corvin is dangerous.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy threatens his family, and the jungle's dangers