crowds. He is backed by cartel money he claims not to notice.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To end the debt-bound order that crushed his family and to be loved by those it crushed.","goal":"Secure a popular acclamation that dissolves the Senate and installs him as First Voice of the isles.","flaw":"Craves adulation and cannot tolerate dissent, so he escalates promises he cannot keep.","internal_conflict":"He knows the forgiven debts are paid by others and that the cartel owns him, yet he tells himself the cause justifies it.","external_conflict":"The Senate, the Wardens and Valeria's schemes all threaten to expose his dependence on cartel gold.","arc":"Rises on promises, then hardens into authoritarianism as the cost of his promises comes due, ending as the kind of ruler he once opposed.","personality_traits":["charismatic","vain","persuasive","volatile"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crowd Oratory","description":"Sways large gatherings with simple, emotionally direct speech.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orsen_fell","name":"Orsen Fell","role":"supporting","description":"Master braider of Emberroost and a veteran Bridge Warden, with burn-scarred forearms and a slow, deliberate manner. He keeps the cloudstone cables safe and distrusts anyone who treats bridges as political leverage.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and the Wardens independent of both Senate and mob.","goal":"Prevent tolls and populist unrest from forcing unsafe bridge repairs.","flaw":"Stubborn literalism that makes him reject compromise even when it would save lives.","internal_conflict":"His oath to the bridges conflicts with his growing sympathy for the labourers Thorne champions.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls under the Toll War starve the Wardens of funds and tempt his own crews to side with Thorne.","arc":"Moves from rigid neutrality to committing the Wardens 