{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_valeria_corvane","name":"Valeria Corvane","role":"protagonist","description":"A former senator of the Aetherian Senate, stripped of her seat after a scandal over unpaid wind-debt that she took on to shield a failing grain convoy. In her fifties, she is gaunt and grey-haired, with a rope-scarred hand from years of crossing skybridges. She lives quietly at Silverspine Academy, where she is tolerated as a guest scholar and watches the Senate she once served be hollowed out.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To redeem her name and stop the Senate from being replaced by acclamation of the crowd.","goal":"Expose and neutralise Cassian Thorne before he can persuade the isles to abolish the Senate.","flaw":"Pride that makes her treat allies as instruments and conceal her plans from them.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her own corruption helped create the conditions in which Thorne thrives, and doubts she deserves to oppose him.","external_conflict":"She must scheme without open resources while the Senate shuns her and Thorne's followers watch the bridges.","arc":"Moves from secretive, self-justifying manoeuvring to accepting accountability, and in the end sacrifices her reputation and position to preserve the Senate's integrity for others.","personality_traits":["calculating","proud","weary","precise"],"abilities":[{"name":"Parliamentary Strategy","description":"Reads votes, procedure and debts to steer Senate outcomes.","category":"social"},{"name":"Cartographic Insight","description":"Uses Academy charts of shifting skybridges to predict movements and routes.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_cassian_thorne","name":"Cassian Thorne","role":"antagonist","description":"A charismatic orator who rose from the docks of Mistral Docks, where he forgave the wind-debts of labourers in the name of the people. Broad-shouldered and weathered, he speaks in plain words that move crowds. He is backed by cartel money he claims not to notice.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To end the debt-bound order that crushed his family and to be loved by those it crushed.","goal":"Secure a popular acclamation that dissolves the Senate and installs him as First Voice of the isles.","flaw":"Craves adulation and cannot tolerate dissent, so he escalates promises he cannot keep.","internal_conflict":"He knows the forgiven debts are paid by others and that the cartel owns him, yet he tells himself the cause justifies it.","external_conflict":"The Senate, the Wardens and Valeria's schemes all threaten to expose his dependence on cartel gold.","arc":"Rises on promises, then hardens into authoritarianism as the cost of his promises comes due, ending as the kind of ruler he once opposed.","personality_traits":["charismatic","vain","persuasive","volatile"],"abilities":[{"name":"Crowd Oratory","description":"Sways large gatherings with simple, emotionally direct speech.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orsen_fell","name":"Orsen Fell","role":"supporting","description":"Master braider of Emberroost and a veteran Bridge Warden, with burn-scarred forearms and a slow, deliberate manner. He keeps the cloudstone cables safe and distrusts anyone who treats bridges as political leverage.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep the skybridges safe and the Wardens independent of both Senate and mob.","goal":"Prevent tolls and populist unrest from forcing unsafe bridge repairs.","flaw":"Stubborn literalism that makes him reject compromise even when it would save lives.","internal_conflict":"His oath to the bridges conflicts with his growing sympathy for the labourers Thorne champions.","external_conflict":"Cartel tolls under the Toll War starve the Wardens of funds and tempt his own crews to side with Thorne.","arc":"Moves from rigid neutrality to committing the Wardens openly to Valeria's cause when safety is threatened.","personality_traits":["steady","blunt","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Braids and inspects skybridge cable with unmatched skill.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_marna_oakhand","name":"Marna Oakhand","role":"supporting","description":"Elder miller of The Hollow and spokesperson for the Hollow Circle. Short and sun-browned, she is patient and observant, and has watched Cartel levies grow heavier each season.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To protect the farmers and millers who feed the archipelago from levy and famine.","goal":"End the Cartel's grain levy without handing power to Thorne.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders that delays alliances she needs.","internal_conflict":"Thorne promises relief from the levy, and she is tempted to accept even though she distrusts him.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy leaves her people short while both the Cartel and Thorne court her support.","arc":"Learns to trust Valeria and leverages the grain supply as a quiet check on Thorne.","personality_traits":["patient","shrewd","wary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Grain Logistics","description":"Knows exactly how grain flows to every isle and where shortages would bite.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_ilvane_rusk","name":"Ilvane Rusk","role":"supporting","description":"A Drift Cartel factor at Mistral Docks who manages Thorne's funding while posing as a mere shipping agent. Elegant and soft-spoken, he sees politics as a ledger.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's monopoly over inter-isle trade through a pliable ruler.","goal":"Keep Thorne dependent on Cartel gold while insulating the Cartel from blame.","flaw":"Contempt for ordinary people leads him to underestimate them.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears Thorne is becoming uncontrollable and may turn on the Cartel.","external_conflict":"Valeria's investigation threatens to trace the funding back to him.","arc":"Moves from confident puppet master to a desperate attempt to cut Thorne loose, and is exposed in the process.","personality_traits":["polished","cold","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Manipulation","description":"Hides payments and debts in routine shipping accounts.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_valeria_thorne_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Valeria Corvane is scheming to bring down Cassian Thorne, whose populist rise she believes will destroy the Senate."},{"id":"rel_thorne_rusk_patron","source_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","target_character_id":"chr_ilvane_rusk","relationship_type":"client","description":"Cassian Thorne depends on Ilvane Rusk's hidden Cartel funding while pretending it does not exist."},{"id":"rel_rusk_thorne_handler","source_character_id":"chr_ilvane_rusk","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","relationship_type":"handler","description":"Ilvane Rusk steers Cassian Thorne's campaign through money, and grows afraid of losing control."},{"id":"rel_valeria_orsen_ally","source_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","target_character_id":"chr_orsen_fell","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Valeria Corvane seeks the support of Orsen Fell and the Wardens, but hides her full plans, straining their trust."},{"id":"rel_marna_valeria_wary","source_character_id":"chr_marna_oakhand","target_character_id":"chr_valeria_corvane","relationship_type":"wary ally","description":"Marna Oakhand distrusts Valeria Corvane as a disgraced senator, yet may trade grain support for protection from the levy."},{"id":"rel_orsen_thorne_rival","source_character_id":"chr_orsen_fell","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_thorne","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Orsen Fell opposes Cassian Thorne's tolls-and-debt promises, which threaten the Wardens' bridge safety work."}]}
