{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_isolde_vane","name":"Isolde Vane","description":"A lean, sun-weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her early thirties, with soot-stained fingers and a braided cloudstone cord wound around her wrist. Raised in the forge-pits of Emberroost, she lost her father to a severed skybridge and has spent her life ensuring no cable fails again.","role":"protagonist","motivation":"To honour her father's death by making the skybridge network unbreakable.","goal":"Forge a binding pact among the Wardens, the Cartel, and the Hollow Circle to defend the bridges against the common enemy.","flaw":"Trusts engineering over people and assumes anyone who disagrees with her is careless.","internal_conflict":"She craves a safe network but suspects true safety may require compromising the Wardens' purity of craft.","external_conflict":"The Toll War makes the Cartel treat her as an enemy, and she must negotiate with them anyway.","arc":"Moves from rigid, solitary perfectionism to a leader who accepts imperfect allies and shared risk.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["driven","meticulous","guarded","stubborn"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Expert at braiding and repairing cloudstone cables under tension.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Spark Discipline","description":"Operates safely around shielded forge-pits and detects fire hazards early.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_dask","name":"Corvin Dask","description":"A silver-tongued Drift Cartel merchant prince in his fifties, wearing layered wind-silk and rings stamped with shipping-lane seals. He rose from dock clerk to guild voice through shrewd deals and quiet blackmail.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's dominion over inter-isle trade permanently.","goal":"Use the alliance to legitimise higher tolls and extend Cartel control over every skybridge.","flaw":"Cannot value anything he cannot price, so he misreads loyalty and sacrifice.","internal_conflict":"He fears the common enemy could destroy his fortune, yet hopes the crisis will make the Cartel indispensable.","external_conflict":"He is pressed by the Toll War with the Wardens and the Grain Levy resistance from the Hollow Circle.","arc":"Begins by exploiting the alliance and ends facing a choice between profit and the survival of the isles.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","patient","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Brokering","description":"Reads shipping routes and leverages wind-debt obligations to bind others.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_maren_holt","name":"Maren Holt","description":"A broad-shouldered miller of the Hollow Circle in her forties, flour in her greying hair and a calm, steady gaze. She survived the memory of the Great Calm through tales of her grandparents and distrusts outsiders' promises.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To keep the Hollow's grain flowing and its people from being taxed into poverty.","goal":"Win an end to the Cartel's grain levy as the price of joining the alliance.","flaw":"Her patience hardens into obstinacy and she refuses to ask for help.","internal_conflict":"She wants to protect the Hollow's quiet independence but sees isolation cannot survive the coming threat.","external_conflict":"The Grain Levy leaves her bargaining against Cartel agents who control the shipping of her harvest.","arc":"Learns to step from the shelter of the Hollow into open leadership of the alliance's food supply.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","personality_traits":["steadfast","practical","wary","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Lore","description":"Predicts wind shifts and storm timing from the turning of the mills.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","description":"A restless young cartographer at Silverspine Academy, ink on his cuffs and a roll of charts always under his arm. A Bridge Warden by affiliation, he charts how the skybridge network drifts and has noticed patterns others ignore.","role":"supporting","motivation":"To prove his theory that the skybridge drift is being manipulated, earning a place among the great cartographers.","goal":"Deliver a complete drift map showing where the common enemy will strike.","flaw":"Reckless with the truth when a discovery is thrilling, and he presents guesses as facts.","internal_conflict":"He longs for scholarly recognition but fears his findings will put friends in danger.","external_conflict":"Academy elders and the Cartel both want to control his charts.","arc":"Grows from an eager prodigy chasing credit into a responsible scholar who tempers certainty with caution.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","personality_traits":["curious","impulsive","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Maps the shifting skybridge network and forecasts future currents.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_dask","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde Vane blames Corvin Dask's rising tolls for starving the Wardens of bridge-repair funds, and their Toll War feud strains every alliance negotiation."},{"id":"rel_corvin_maren_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_dask","target_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvin Dask enforces the Cartel's Grain Levy on Maren Holt's harvests, and she in turn treats him as a predator she must outlast."},{"id":"rel_isolde_tobias_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Isolde Vane mentors fellow Warden Tobias Wren, tempering his reckless theories with engineering discipline."},{"id":"rel_maren_isolde_ally","source_character_id":"chr_maren_holt","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Holt reluctantly allies with Isolde Vane because the Wardens' bridges are the only way the Hollow's grain reaches the other isles."}]}
