{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","description":"A weathered Bridge Warden engineer in her late thirties, born on Emberroost to a family of cable-braiders. She has a burn-scarred left forearm from a forge-pit accident, close-cropped grey-streaked hair, and soot-stained leathers. After years inspecting skybridge anchor points, she is the first to notice that the collapse of the central span was sabotage rather than wear.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To honour the crew she lost when the central span failed and to ensure no one else dies on a bridge she certified safe.","goal":"Prove the central span was deliberately severed and expose who profited from it.","flaw":"She trusts only her own inspections and refuses to delegate or admit that she can be wrong.","internal_conflict":"She suspects her own signed safety certificate may have missed the damage, and fears she is partly responsible.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's tolls and the Wardens' own leadership both pressure her to blame a convenient scapegoat and close the case quickly.","arc":"Maren begins as a solitary, guilt-driven inspector, learns to share evidence and authority with former rivals across the isles, and ends as a unifying figure who accepts shared responsibility for the network.","personality_traits":["meticulous","stubborn","grim","loyal","dry-humoured"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Reading","description":"Can diagnose stress and tampering in cloudstone cable by touch and sound.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Forge-pit Discipline","description":"Trained to work safely around shielded flame and spot violations of the no-open-flame rule.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_corvin_adler","name":"Corvin Adler","description":"A sleek, middle-aged Drift Cartel factor operating from Mistral Docks, with rings of braided wind-debt tokens on every finger and a quiet, courteous voice. He rose from dockhand to shipping-lane broker by trading in other people's debts.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To lock the archipelago into dependence on Cartel-controlled routes so he can never again be a debtor himself.","goal":"Use the collapse of the central span to justify Cartel-run tolls and a monopoly on the remaining crossings.","flaw":"He cannot believe anyone acts without a price, so he constantly underestimates sincere opponents.","internal_conflict":"He privately knows the sabotage will kill people he once worked beside on the docks, yet tells himself it is just commerce.","external_conflict":"Cartel rivals and the Hollow Circle's resistance to the grain levy threaten to expose his dealings.","arc":"Corvin tightens his grip as the investigation closes in, but his miscalculation about the united isles leads to his exposure and the loss of the power he built.","personality_traits":["polished","calculating","patient","paranoid"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Ledger Mastery","description":"Tracks and leverages wind-debts across hundreds of people from memory.","category":"social"},{"name":"Lane Control","description":"Directs shipping lanes to starve or favour entire isles.","category":"other"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_quill","name":"Isolde Quill","description":"A young cartographer at Silverspine Academy with ink-stained fingers, round spectacles, and a habit of sketching the drift of every isle on her sleeves. She charted the network that the collapsed span belonged to.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove that careful mapping can save lives and justify the Academy's place in a harsh world.","goal":"Reconstruct the drift patterns on the night of the collapse to show the span was cut at a precise moment.","flaw":"She is naive about power and shares her findings with anyone who flatters her curiosity.","internal_conflict":"Her ambition for recognition conflicts with her duty to keep dangerous findings secret.","external_conflict":"Academy elders, dependent on Cartel funding, forbid her from publishing her charts.","arc":"Isolde moves from idealistic scholar to a cautious, courageous witness who publishes her maps despite the risk.","personality_traits":["curious","earnest","quick-witted","anxious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Drift Charting","description":"Predicts the movement of isles and skybridge tension from observational data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_hale","name":"Tobias Hale","description":"A broad, soft-spoken miller of the Hollow Circle with flour-dusted forearms and a deep laugh that has grown rare. He leads his village's windmill cooperative and carries the burden of feeding isles that now cannot be reached.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and protect his village from being bled by the Cartel levy.","goal":"Reopen a safe grain route and break the Cartel's levy without starting a war.","flaw":"His stubborn pacifism makes him slow to act when decisive action is needed.","internal_conflict":"He remembers the Great Calm and fears that fighting back will repeat its suffering, yet inaction is starving his neighbours.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers demand levy payments while the broken bridge strands his harvest.","arc":"Tobias shifts from reluctant neutrality to leading the Hollow Circle into an open alliance with the Wardens.","personality_traits":["gentle","patient","resilient","reserved"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Builds and repairs windmills that work through the lowest winds.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Village Trust","description":"Commands deep loyalty among the Hollow's farmers.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_sable_rook","name":"Sable Rook","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed skyrunner at Mistral Docks who ferries cargo and rumours across unlicensed routes. She wears a patched wind-cloak and carries a shielded lantern, always careful to avoid open flame. She was on the central span hours before it fell.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","motivation":"To pay off a crushing wind-debt held by the Cartel and win her freedom to fly where she chooses.","goal":"Sell what she saw on the night of the collapse for enough to clear her debt.","flaw":"She treats loyalty as a transaction and flees when things get dangerous.","internal_conflict":"She wants to stay free of everyone, but her conscience will not let her bury what she witnessed.","external_conflict":"Corvin Adler holds her debt and would silence her if he learned what she saw.","arc":"Sable starts as a self-interested smuggler, is forced to choose between her freedom and the truth, and ends by testifying and guiding the Wardens' investigation.","personality_traits":["cunning","restless","sardonic","brave under pressure"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skyrunning","description":"Navigates unlit, unmapped wind currents between isles at speed.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Street Network","description":"Knows dockside informants and smuggler routes.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_corvin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_adler","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maren Voss is investigating the sabotage that Corvin Adler stands to profit from, making them direct adversaries over the truth of the central span's collapse."},{"id":"rel_corvin_sable_creditor","source_character_id":"chr_corvin_adler","target_character_id":"chr_sable_rook","relationship_type":"creditor","description":"Corvin Adler holds Sable Rook's wind-debt and uses it to control her, threatening her if she reveals what she saw."},{"id":"rel_isolde_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_quill","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Quill supplies Maren Voss with drift charts that support the sabotage theory, while Maren protects her from Academy censure."},{"id":"rel_tobias_corvin_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_hale","target_character_id":"chr_corvin_adler","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobias Hale resists the grain levy that Corvin Adler enforces, putting the Hollow Circle in direct conflict with the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_sable_maren_uneasy_ally","source_character_id":"chr_sable_rook","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Sable Rook reluctantly shares her eyewitness account with Maren Voss, though she distrusts the Wardens and may flee if pressed."}]}
