[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","description":"A weathered senior Bridge Warden in her forties, raised on Emberroost among the cable-braiders. Her hands are scarred from cloudstone fibre and her grey-streaked hair is bound tight against the wind. She has spent two decades inspecting the old protective wards stitched into the skybridge anchors, which are the oldest safeguards of the realm and are now failing. She wears a soot-stained leather coat and carries a tally-rod of knotted cord.","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","role":"protagonist","motivation":"To keep the people who cross the bridges alive, as her brother was lost when an anchor ward failed in her youth.","goal":"Find the cause of the failing wards and reinforce every anchor ward before the next storm season.","flaw":"Stubborn pride; she distrusts anyone outside the Wardens and hides how bad the failures truly are.","internal_conflict":"She wonders whether the realm's rigid prohibition on arcane power is what made the wards impossible to renew.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel's rising tolls starve the Wardens of funds and labour, while the failing wards worsen each season.","arc":"Maren moves from secretive self-reliance to forging an uneasy coalition across factions, accepting a costly truth about the realm's laws and choosing to expose it to save the bridges.","personality_traits":["stubborn","dutiful","observant","guarded","grim"],"abilities":[{"name":"Anchor Inspection","description":"Reads strain and decay in cloudstone cables by touch and sound.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Cable Braiding","description":"Expert at splicing and repairing skybridge cables under wind load.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_oren_thale","name":"Oren Thale","description":"A lean, sharp-eyed cartographer at Silverspine Academy, in his thirties, with ink-stained cuffs and a nervous habit of re-rolling charts. He has noticed that the bridge network's shifts correlate with the failing wards and keeps the data in a locked drawer.","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","role":"supporting","motivation":"To prove his theory and earn a place among respected scholars after years of being dismissed.","goal":"Publish a complete chart showing where and when each ward will fail.","flaw":"Cowardice when confronted by authority; he withholds findings rather than risk punishment.","internal_conflict":"He knows his charts could save lives but fears they will also implicate the Academy and himself.","external_conflict":"The Academy's masters suppress research that questions the kingdom's founding laws.","arc":"Oren overcomes his fear, giving Maren his data and publicly defending it, trading his safety for credibility.","personality_traits":["meticulous","anxious","curious","analytical"],"abilities":[{"name":"Network Charting","description":"Predicts skybridge drift patterns from years of survey data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_castor_drell","name":"Castor Drell","description":"A silver-tongued merchant prince of the Drift Cartel in his fifties, broad and immaculately dressed, who runs the shipping lanes out of Mistral Docks. He has funded his rise on skybridge tolls and quietly profits from every failing crossing.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","role":"antagonist","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's permanent monopoly over all travel and trade between the isles.","goal":"Raise tolls and shift traffic onto Cartel-owned ships as the bridges grow unsafe.","flaw":"Greed and contempt for anyone he cannot buy, which blinds him to risks beyond profit.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears a collapse of the bridges would ruin the very trade he built.","external_conflict":"The Wardens and the Hollow Circle resist his tolls and levies, and Maren threatens to expose his dealings.","arc":"Castor escalates his schemes as the wards fail, and is finally forced to choose between his monopoly and the realm's survival, ending ruined or reluctantly complicit in the repair.","personality_traits":["charming","ruthless","calculating","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Trade Leverage","description":"Binds debtors through wind-debt and contracts to secure loyalty.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_isolde_march","name":"Isolde March","description":"A sturdy miller and elder of the Hollow Circle in her sixties, with flour-dusted forearms and a calm, measured voice. She has watched the windmills of The Hollow feed half the archipelago through lean seasons since the Great Calm was still living memory among her elders.","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","role":"supporting","motivation":"To protect her community from hunger and exploitation.","goal":"Defeat the Cartel's grain levy without starting open violence.","flaw":"Overcaution; she delays decisive action and lets problems fester.","internal_conflict":"She must choose between keeping the Circle's quiet neutrality and joining a fight that may cost lives.","external_conflict":"The Cartel levy threatens to empty The Hollow's granaries before winter.","arc":"Isolde leaves neutrality behind, uniting the farmers with the Wardens and supplying the repair effort at great risk to her people.","personality_traits":["patient","wise","cautious","maternal"],"abilities":[{"name":"Community Leadership","description":"Mediates disputes and rallies farmers and millers behind a shared cause.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_pell_corvin","name":"Pell Corvin","description":"A wiry young dockhand and courier at Mistral Docks, barely twenty, with a quick grin and a patched coat. He runs messages and cargo between isles and has seen Cartel crews moving crates away from failing bridges in secret.","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","role":"supporting","motivation":"To escape wind-debt that has bound his family to the Cartel for generations.","goal":"Earn enough from courier work to clear his family's debt.","flaw":"Impulsive and easily tempted by quick money.","internal_conflict":"He is torn between loyalty to his Cartel-employed family and the conscience that urges him to reveal what he has seen.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers watch him, and his debt keeps him under Castor's thumb.","arc":"Pell goes from opportunistic courier to a brave witness, carrying Maren's evidence across the isles at personal risk.","personality_traits":["quick-witted","reckless","loyal","resourceful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windrunning","description":"Navigates crowded docks and skybridges at speed in rough weather.","category":"physical"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_castor_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_castor_drell","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Maren Voss opposes Castor Drell, whose tolls starve the Wardens and whose profits depend on the bridges' failures she fights to prevent."},{"id":"rel_maren_oren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_oren_thale","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Maren Voss relies on Oren Thale's charts to predict ward failures, though she distrusts his timidity."},{"id":"rel_castor_pell_master","source_character_id":"chr_castor_drell","target_character_id":"chr_pell_corvin","relationship_type":"master","description":"Castor Drell holds Pell Corvin's family in wind-debt and uses him as an errand runner, tightening his control as Pell grows suspicious."},{"id":"rel_isolde_castor_opponent","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_march","target_character_id":"chr_castor_drell","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Isolde March resists Castor Drell's grain levy, creating friction that threatens The Hollow's quiet neutrality."},{"id":"rel_pell_maren_informant","source_character_id":"chr_pell_corvin","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Pell Corvin secretly passes Maren Voss what he has seen of Cartel crews, risking Castor Drell's retaliation."},{"id":"rel_isolde_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_march","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde March and Maren Voss form a wary partnership, trading grain and labour for bridge repairs against the Cartel."}]}
</Output>
