{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_maren_voss","name":"Maren Voss","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A thirty-four-year-old Bridge Warden cable-braider from Emberroost, lean and soot-freckled, with scarred forearms from years in the shielded forge-pits. She keeps a strand of cloudstone thread knotted around her wrist. After a sleepless season she begins to see the same dream as everyone around her, a dream that seems to come from a luminous dreamstone found in a cloudstone seam.","motivation":"To protect the people of the isles from a danger she alone recognises in the shared dreams.","goal":"Trace the dreamstone to its source and decide whether to seal it away before its dreams spread beyond the isles.","flaw":"She trusts her own judgment over the counsel of others and hides what she fears.","internal_conflict":"She is drawn to the comfort of the shared dream, where her dead brother appears, even as she knows it is hollowing out her waking mind.","external_conflict":"The Wardens' leadership wants the stone studied in place, while the Drift Cartel wants it moved, and Maren must cross skybridges whose wind-debt she can barely pay.","arc":"Maren moves from solitary secrecy and denial to accepting help and grief, and ultimately chooses to confront the dreamstone openly, trading her private dream for the community's waking safety.","personality_traits":["stubborn","observant","dryly funny","guilt-ridden"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone braiding","description":"Expert at reading tension and fault lines in woven skybridge cable.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Dream lucidity","description":"Can sometimes recognise she is inside the shared dream and steer her actions there.","category":"supernatural"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_hale","name":"Orsolya Hale","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","description":"A silver-haired Cartel merchant princess in her fifties, precise and soft-spoken, who dresses in dove-grey coats stitched with shipping-lane charts. She built her fortune on tolls and sees the dreamstone as the next monopoly: a product that people will pay anything to dream with.","motivation":"To secure the Cartel's dominance and her own family's legacy against the rising cost of the Toll War.","goal":"Seize control of the dreamstone and license access to its dreams across the archipelago.","flaw":"She treats every person and wonder as an asset to be priced.","internal_conflict":"She privately dreads being forgotten, and the dream shows her a life in which her estranged daughter still loves her.","external_conflict":"The Wardens oppose her tolls and the Hollow Circle resists her grain levy, leaving her short of allies and short of time.","arc":"Orsolya escalates from quiet commercial pressure to coercion, then is undone when the dream exposes her loneliness to the whole colony, forcing a reckoning with what she has traded away.","personality_traits":["calculating","polite","patient","lonely"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane control","description":"Commands shipping schedules and debt ledgers that can strand or enrich entire isles.","category":"social"},{"name":"Debt reading","description":"Quickly gauges what a person owes and what they will give to clear it.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_tobias_wren","name":"Tobias Wren","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","description":"A twenty-six-year-old cartographer at Silverspine Academy, ink-stained and restless, with a habit of sketching in the margins of every chart. He maps where the dreams are strongest and notices the pattern follows the skybridge network.","motivation":"To prove that the dreams follow measurable patterns and are not madness.","goal":"Complete a chart of the dream's spread that predicts where it will surface next.","flaw":"He is so absorbed in data that he overlooks the people suffering inside it.","internal_conflict":"He wants academic recognition but suspects his findings could be used by the Cartel to exploit the stone.","external_conflict":"Academy elders dismiss his charts, and the Cartel offers funding that would compromise them.","arc":"Tobias shifts from detached mapper to engaged ally, choosing to publish his findings openly rather than sell them.","personality_traits":["curious","anxious","meticulous","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Pattern charting","description":"Detects shifts in the skybridge and dream networks from scattered observations.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_edda_marsh","name":"Edda Marsh","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","description":"An elderly miller of the Hollow, broad-shouldered with flour-dusted hands and clouded eyes, who remembers the Great Calm. She is the first to say the dreams feel like the stillness returning.","motivation":"To keep her community fed, calm, and out of the Cartel's debt.","goal":"Persuade the Hollow Circle to refuse the Cartel levy and stay united against the dreamstone's pull.","flaw":"She clings to old fears and resists any new way of doing things.","internal_conflict":"She longs for the quiet of the dream, yet distrusts anything that comes without a cost.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's grain levy and the dream's spread both strain her people's unity.","arc":"Edda moves from stubborn isolation to lending the Hollow's resources and wisdom to Maren's cause, bridging the isles she once distrusted.","personality_traits":["wise","blunt","protective","wary"],"abilities":[{"name":"Weather sense","description":"Reads wind and stillness, noticing when the air itself feels wrong.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Community standing","description":"Her word can rally the Hollow's farmers and millers.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_maren_orsolya_rivalry","source_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","target_character_id":"chr_orsolya_hale","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Maren Voss opposes Orsolya Hale because Orsolya wants to seize and sell the dreamstone that Maren wants sealed, and their factions are already locked in the Toll War."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_maren_pressure","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_hale","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Orsolya Hale presses Maren Voss with wind-debt and bribes, treating her as the obstacle between the Cartel and the dreamstone."},{"id":"rel_tobias_maren_ally","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Tobias Wren supplies Maren Voss with charts of the dream's spread, and Maren in turn protects his research from Cartel interference."},{"id":"rel_edda_maren_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_edda_marsh","target_character_id":"chr_maren_voss","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Edda Marsh draws on her memory of the Great Calm to counsel Maren Voss about the cost of comforting stillness."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_tobias_temptation","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_hale","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_wren","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Orsolya Hale tempts Tobias Wren with funding for his charts, hoping to turn his findings into a Cartel map of the dreamstone."}]}
