ckhand at Mistral Docks to master of three fleets, and is charming, patient, and ruthless. He backs a puppet claimant to the throne so the Cartel can write the laws of the sky.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To secure permanent Cartel control of every shipping lane and bridge crossing so he never again faces poverty.","goal":"Place his chosen claimant on the throne and enshrine the Cartel's tolls and grain levy in law.","flaw":"Greed so total that he treats every person as a debt to be collected.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears that his wealth has made him hollow, yet he cannot stop accumulating.","external_conflict":"Wardens, farmers, and rival royal houses all resist the Toll War and the Grain Levy he is pushing.","arc":"Corvane's escalating grip on the isles overreaches until his own allies turn on him, forcing a reckoning with the cost of his wind-debts.","personality_traits":["charming","patient","calculating","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Lane Mastery","description":"Reads wind currents and trade flows to predict where cargo and power will move.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Binds rivals through wind-debts and favors until they cannot refuse him.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","name":"Tamsin Orrel","description":"A broad-shouldered Hollow Circle miller in her late twenties, with flour-dusted hair tied under a faded scarf and calloused hands. She runs the largest windmill on The Hollow and keeps the Great Calm's lessons alive in her village's grain stores. She is warm, blunt, and quietly trusted by farmers across the isles.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep the archipelago fed and her neighbors free from Cartel debt.","goal":"Break the Cartel's Grain Levy by building a farmer-run shipping network.","flaw":"Naive trust in people who speak kindly, which has been exploited before.","internal_conflict":"She wants peace for her village but is drawn toward open resistance that could bring reprisals.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens to bankrupt The Hollow and starve smaller isles.","arc":"Tamsin grows from a reluctant local miller into a hardened leader of the Hollow Circle, learning to pair her warmth with caution.","personality_traits":["warm","blunt","resilient","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Knows how to tune mills to scarce winds and stretch grain supplies.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Village Trust","description":"Farmers across the isles listen to her and share information freely.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_aurelio_pell","name":"Aurelio Pell","description":"A thin, ink-stained cartographer at Silverspine Academy, forty-five, who wears round brass spectacles and carries a case of charting tools. He spent years mapping the shifting skybridge network and has recently found drift patterns that suggest something stirring in the cold, icy depths below the isles. Scholarly and anxious, he is more comfortable with maps than people.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove his chart of an awakening threat beneath the ice before it is too late.","goal":"Convince the houses to pause their war and prepare for the ancient enemy rising under the ice.","flaw":"Cowardice and a habit of hedging his findings until nobody listens.","internal_conflict":"He fears ridicule and political retaliation but knows silence will doom the isles.","external_conflict":"The warring houses dismiss his warnings as a ploy, and the Cartel wants his maps for its own ends.","arc":"Aurelio overcomes his timidity to stand before the royal houses and present his evidence, becoming the voice that unites them against the ice enemy.","personality_traits":["anxious","brilliant","precise","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Charts drifting isles and predicts how the bridge network will shift.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Pattern Reading","description":"Spots anomalies in wind and ice data that hint at hidden dangers.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_serrin_halloway","name":"Serrin Halloway","description":"A quick-witted dock pilot in her early twenties with sun-bleached hair and a scarred wind-skiff, working out of Mistral Docks. She runs unlicensed cargo past Cartel toll stations and knows every back-lane in the archipelago. Charming and reckless, she was raised by Cartel dockhands yet resents their masters.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To escape the wind-debt that her family has owed the Cartel for three generations.","goal":"Earn enough from smuggling and guiding Isolde to clear her family's debt for good.","flaw":"Recklessness and a habit of lying even when the truth would serve her better.","internal_conflict":"She is loyal to the dockhands who raised her but is betraying the Cartel they serve.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers are hunting her skiff, and her debt grows with every crossing.","arc":"Serrin shifts from selfish smuggler to committed ally, choosing to guide the rebellion even when it costs her the chance to clear her own debt.","personality_traits":["reckless","witty","resourceful","evasive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Back-Lane Piloting","description":"Navigates wind currents and hidden routes that avoid toll stations.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Fast Talk","description":"Bluffs and bargains her way past inspectors and guards.","category":"social"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_isolde_corvane_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterra","target_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Isolde Vanterra opposes Corvane Dray because his Cartel tolls and assassins threaten the skybridges and her claim; the Toll War drives their conflict."},{"id":"rel_corvane_isolde_hunter","source_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterra","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Corvane Dray sees Isolde Vanterra as the one claimant who could break the Cartel's control, so he sends agents to find and discredit her."},{"id":"rel_isolde_tamsin_ally","source_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterra","target_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Isolde Vanterra and Tamsin Orrel join forces as Wardens and farmers against the Cartel's tolls and Grain Levy."},{"id":"rel_aurelio_isolde_mentor","source_character_id":"chr_aurelio_pell","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterra","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Aurelio Pell guides Isolde Vanterra with his charts and warnings about the ice enemy, pushing her to see beyond the throne war."},{"id":"rel_serrin_isolde_ally","source_character_id":"chr_serrin_halloway","target_character_id":"chr_isolde_vanterra","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Serrin Halloway guides Isolde Vanterra through hidden lanes past Cartel toll stations in exchange for a chance at clearing her family's debt."},{"id":"rel_corvane_serrin_enemy","source_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","target_character_id":"chr_serrin_halloway","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Corvane Dray holds Serrin Halloway's family debt and sends enforcers after her as she defies the Cartel."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_corvane_rival","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_orrel","target_character_id":"chr_corvane_dray","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tamsin Orrel resists Corvane Dray's Grain Levy and organizes Hollow Circle farmers against his shipping monopoly."}]}
