h has been exploited before.","internal_conflict":"She wants peace for her village but is drawn toward open resistance that could bring reprisals.","external_conflict":"The Cartel's levy threatens to bankrupt The Hollow and starve smaller isles.","arc":"Tamsin grows from a reluctant local miller into a hardened leader of the Hollow Circle, learning to pair her warmth with caution.","personality_traits":["warm","blunt","resilient","generous"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windmill Craft","description":"Knows how to tune mills to scarce winds and stretch grain supplies.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Village Trust","description":"Farmers across the isles listen to her and share information freely.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_aurelio_pell","name":"Aurelio Pell","description":"A thin, ink-stained cartographer at Silverspine Academy, forty-five, who wears round brass spectacles and carries a case of charting tools. He spent years mapping the shifting skybridge network and has recently found drift patterns that suggest something stirring in the cold, icy depths below the isles. Scholarly and anxious, he is more comfortable with maps than people.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To prove his chart of an awakening threat beneath the ice before it is too late.","goal":"Convince the houses to pause their war and prepare for the ancient enemy rising under the ice.","flaw":"Cowardice and a habit of hedging his findings until nobody listens.","internal_conflict":"He fears ridicule and political retaliation but knows silence will doom the isles.","external_conflict":"The warring houses dismiss his warnings as a ploy, and the Cartel wants his maps for its own ends.","arc":"Aurelio overcomes his timidity to stand before the royal houses and present his evidence, becoming the voice that unites them against the ice enemy.","personality_traits":["anxious","brilliant","precise","idealistic"],"abilities":[{"name":