{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_odalys_venn","name":"Odalys Venn","description":"A retired Silverspine Academy cartographer in her late fifties, silver-haired and sharp-eyed, who carries a brass folding rule and a notebook of skybridge sketches. Invited to the weekend party at the manor as an old friend of the host, she is known for noticing what others overlook.","role":"protagonist","motivation":"She believes a map is only honest if every blank space is filled, and she cannot leave an unexplained death uncharted.","goal":"Identify the murderer before the skybridge crossing home reopens at the end of the weekend.","flaw":"Her curiosity makes her intrusive, and she often voices accusations before she has proof.","internal_conflict":"She fears her sharpness is fading with age and that she will name the wrong person.","external_conflict":"The guests close ranks against her prying, and the manor's steward wants the matter left to the Wardens.","arc":"She begins as a self-doubting busybody. She learns to weigh evidence patiently, and she ends by revealing the culprit with quiet confidence.","personality_traits":["observant","dry-witted","stubborn","kind"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cartographer's Eye","description":"Spots inconsistencies in layouts, distances and timelines, such as a room that is too short for its walls.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Gentle Interrogation","description":"Draws confessions out of guests with tea and small talk.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_cassian_rook","name":"Cassian Rook","description":"A smooth, middle-aged Drift Cartel merchant prince with rings on every finger and a perfectly trimmed beard. He is the host of the weekend and owns the manor, and he has grown rich on skybridge tolls.","role":"supporting","motivation":"He wants to secure a lasting Cartel monopoly on the manor's private landing stages.","goal":"Close a secret toll agreement over the weekend without the other guests learning of it.","flaw":"Arrogance leads him to treat everyone as a buyer or a rival.","internal_conflict":"He is ashamed that his fortune rests on debts he has quietly forgiven and then called in again.","external_conflict":"The Toll War has made enemies of the Wardens and farmers among his guests.","arc":"He is the apparent first suspect and then the victim of events. His secrets surface, and his reputation is reshaped.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain"],"abilities":[{"name":"Silver Tongue","description":"Negotiates deals and smooths over scandal.","category":"social"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel"},{"id":"chr_wynn_ashgrove","name":"Wynn Ashgrove","description":"A broad-shouldered miller from The Hollow in her forties, flour still in the creases of her hands. She is warm and blunt, and she came to the manor to petition against the Grain Levy.","role":"supporting","motivation":"She wants to protect the Hollow Circle's farmers from ruinous Cartel levies.","goal":"Get Cassian Rook to withdraw the grain levy in writing.","flaw":"A hot temper that makes her say threats she does not mean.","internal_conflict":"She is torn between honest petition and the desperate wish to hurt the man starving her neighbours.","external_conflict":"Her public threat against Cassian makes her the obvious suspect.","arc":"She is wrongly suspected and then cleared. She learns that patient allies serve her cause better than anger.","personality_traits":["warm","blunt","loyal","fiery"],"abilities":[{"name":"Miller's Strength","description":"Lifts heavy sacks and doors that others cannot.","category":"physical"}],"home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle"},{"id":"chr_tobias_quill","name":"Tobias Quill","description":"A nervous young Bridge Warden engineer from Emberroost, thin and ink-stained. He carries a leather satchel of cable-tension tables and avoids eye contact.","role":"antagonist","motivation":"He needs to hide that he falsified a cable inspection which later endangered a skybridge.","goal":"Recover and destroy the incriminating inspection ledger kept in the manor's study.","flaw":"Cowardice that makes him panic and lie.","internal_conflict":"His conscience gnaws at him even as he protects himself.","external_conflict":"Odalys's investigation threatens to expose his forged ledger, and the wind-debt he owes Cassian leaves him under pressure.","arc":"He moves from desperate concealment to the crime itself. His guilt then breaks him into confession.","personality_traits":["anxious","meticulous","secretive"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cable Knowledge","description":"Understands braided cloudstone and how to sabotage or repair a rigging.","category":"technological"}],"home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens"},{"id":"chr_marguerite_dane","name":"Marguerite Dane","description":"The manor's long-serving steward, a composed woman in her sixties in a grey livery. She knows every key, passage and secret of the house.","role":"supporting","motivation":"She wants to preserve the manor's dignity and her own position after years of service.","goal":"Keep the guests calm and the household's secrets private until the Wardens arrive.","flaw":"Excessive discretion leads her to withhold important facts.","internal_conflict":"Loyalty to Cassian conflicts with her duty to tell the truth.","external_conflict":"Odalys presses her for details she is unwilling to give.","arc":"She guards silence at first. She eventually shares what she saw and becomes the key witness.","personality_traits":["composed","loyal","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"House Memory","description":"Remembers who went where and when across the whole manor.","category":"mental"}],"home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks"}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_odalys_tobias","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_venn","target_character_id":"chr_tobias_quill","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Odalys Venn, the veteran cartographer, gradually closes in on Tobias Quill, whose forged inspection ledger she suspects, and this pressure pushes him toward desperate acts."},{"id":"rel_cassian_wynn","source_character_id":"chr_wynn_ashgrove","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_rook","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Wynn Ashgrove blames Cassian Rook for the Grain Levy that threatens her neighbours, and her public threats make her the obvious suspect."},{"id":"rel_tobias_cassian","source_character_id":"chr_tobias_quill","target_character_id":"chr_cassian_rook","relationship_type":"debtor","description":"Tobias Quill owes Cassian Rook a heavy wind-debt, and Cassian uses it as leverage over the engineer."},{"id":"rel_odalys_marguerite","source_character_id":"chr_odalys_venn","target_character_id":"chr_marguerite_dane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Odalys Venn coaxes testimony from Marguerite Dane, whose knowledge of the manor becomes the key to solving the case."}]}
