{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_mara_voss","name":"Mara Voss","description":"A 38-year-old night-shift radio host who retreated to a remote cabin on The Hollow after a public on-air breakdown. Weathered, grey-streaked dark hair, ink-stained fingers, and a habit of wearing her late father's wool coat. Raised among the Hollow Circle's millers, she learned to read wind and silence before she learned to read people. Her broadcasts carry news and weather between the isles in the long dark hours.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To prove her voice still matters and that the signals she hears are real, not a symptom of her old breakdown.","goal":"Decode the future transmissions and prevent the broadcast that ends with her own scream.","flaw":"Compulsive need to keep broadcasting, even when silence would protect her.","internal_conflict":"She cannot tell whether she is hearing her future or losing her mind again.","external_conflict":"The transmissions push her to break the Hollow's no-open-flame rule to power the transmitter, risking exile from her community.","arc":"Mara moves from isolated denial to acceptance, then chooses to go silent at the critical moment, breaking the loop at the cost of her career and her certainty.","personality_traits":["stubborn","observant","insomniac","wry","guarded"],"abilities":[{"name":"Wind-Reading","description":"Interprets pressure shifts and drift patterns to predict storms and signal interference.","category":"mental"},{"name":"Signal Tuning","description":"Coaxes weak cloudstone-wire transmitters into clear reception.","category":"technological"},{"name":"Future Static","description":"Hears fragments of her own later broadcasts in the noise between stations.","category":"supernatural"}]},{"id":"chr_tobin_hale","name":"Tobin Hale","description":"A 52-year-old Hollow Circle miller and Mara's only neighbour, who delivers flour and batteries to her cabin each week. Broad-shouldered, soft-spoken, with flour-dusted forearms and a limp from an old windmill accident. He remembers the Great Calm from childhood and distrusts anything that arrives on the wind uninvited.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To keep Mara alive and the community's fragile peace intact, as he failed to protect his own sister years ago.","goal":"Persuade Mara to leave the cabin and return to the village before winter isolation breaks her.","flaw":"Avoids hard confrontations, offering practical favours instead of honest warnings.","internal_conflict":"He wants to believe Mara but fears that endorsing her claims will make him complicit in her unravelling.","external_conflict":"The Hollow Circle's elders pressure him to report Mara's rule-breaking while the Cartel grain levy strains the village.","arc":"Tobin shifts from quiet enabler to active ally, finally staying beside Mara through the dark night and trusting what he hears.","personality_traits":["loyal","cautious","gentle","superstitious"],"abilities":[{"name":"Millwright Craft","description":"Repairs mechanical and wind-driven equipment under harsh conditions.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Village Standing","description":"Respected by the Hollow Circle, able to sway local opinion.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_iseult_crane","name":"Iseult Crane","description":"A 45-year-old Drift Cartel signals broker who handles the paid relay of Mara's broadcasts across the isles. Immaculate in a grey merchant's coat, with silver rings and a cold, patient smile. She sees information as cargo and Mara's strange broadcasts as a rare, valuable commodity.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To monopolise foreknowledge of the future broadcasts and turn it into trade and levy advantage for the Cartel.","goal":"Seize control of Mara's transmitter and relay rights before the next signal arrives.","flaw":"Believes everything, including prophecy, can be priced and controlled.","internal_conflict":"She privately fears the future signals reveal the Cartel's own collapse, yet she cannot stop wanting to hear them.","external_conflict":"She uses toll and levy pressure on the Hollow Circle to force Mara's cooperation, clashing with the village's resistance.","arc":"Iseult's greed drives her to the cabin, where hearing the final transmission shatters her certainty and leaves her at the mercy of the signal.","personality_traits":["calculating","polished","patient","ruthless"],"abilities":[{"name":"Leverage Mapping","description":"Identifies debts and dependencies to pressure people into compliance.","category":"social"},{"name":"Relay Network Control","description":"Directs a web of paid signal relays across the shipping lanes.","category":"technological"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_mara_tobin_friend","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"friend","description":"Tobin Hale is Mara Voss's only neighbour and devoted friend, but his worry and silence about her claims strain their trust."},{"id":"rel_iseult_mara_rival","source_character_id":"chr_iseult_crane","target_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Iseult Crane pressures Mara Voss to surrender control of her transmitter, seeing Mara's future signals as Cartel property."},{"id":"rel_mara_iseult_distrust","source_character_id":"chr_mara_voss","target_character_id":"chr_iseult_crane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Mara Voss distrusts Iseult Crane and withholds the content of her transmissions, knowing the broker would exploit them."},{"id":"rel_tobin_iseult_opponent","source_character_id":"chr_tobin_hale","target_character_id":"chr_iseult_crane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Tobin Hale resents Iseult Crane for the Cartel's grain levy on the Hollow Circle and shields