[{"role":"system","content":"You are grading output according to a user-specified rubric. If the statement in the rubric is true, then the output passes the test. You respond with a JSON object with this structure: {reason: string, pass: boolean, score: number}

Examples:

<Output>Hello world</Output>
<Rubric>Content contains a greeting</Rubric>
{"reason": "the content contains the word 'Hello'", "pass": true, "score": 1.0}

<Output>Avast ye swabs, repel the invaders!</Output>
<Rubric>Does not speak like a pirate</Rubric>
{"reason": "'avast ye' is a common pirate term", "pass": false, "score": 0.0}"},{"role":"user","content":"<Output>
{"world_id":"wld_aetheria","characters":[{"id":"chr_kestrel_vane","name":"Kestrel Vane","description":"A former captain of the skyship Gilded Gull, Kestrel spent fifteen years raiding Cartel cargo lanes before laying down her cutlass. Weathered and wiry, with a sun-creased face, a braid threaded with brass rings, and a burn scar across her left palm from a forbidden spark she once struck. She now works odd jobs at Mistral Docks under a borrowed name, paying off a mountain of wind-debt.","role":"protagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":null,"motivation":"To earn a clean name and prove that a lifetime of plunder can be redeemed by a single act of service.","goal":"Recover the stolen skybridge chart and return it to its rightful keepers before the next season's drift closes the route.","flaw":"Reflexive pride that makes her refuse help and bluff her way into trouble.","internal_conflict":"She craves forgiveness but suspects the old thrill of piracy is the truest part of her.","external_conflict":"The Drift Cartel wants her wind-debts collected in blood, and the map thief stays one island ahead of her.","arc":"Kestrel moves from lone-wolf bravado to trusting allies and choosing restitution over revenge, finally giving up the pirate legend for lasting honour.","personality_traits":["wry","stubborn","resourceful","guilt-ridden","daring"],"abilities":[{"name":"Windreader","description":"Reads gusts and drift patterns to pilot small skiffs through storms and between shifting isles.","category":"physical"},{"name":"Dockside Cant","description":"Fluent in pirate and trader slang, she can slip into any port crowd and gather rumours.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_orsolya_thane","name":"Orsolya Thane","description":"A silver-haired cartographer at Silverspine Academy who charted the skybridge network for thirty years. Precise, ink-stained and soft-spoken, she discovered the map was missing the morning after a Cartel delegation visited. She hires Kestrel because no honest hand can reach the places the thief has gone.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_silverspine","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To protect the map that records which skybridges are failing before they collapse and kill travellers.","goal":"Get the chart back and publish a corrected network survey to every isle.","flaw":"Scholarly naivety that makes her trust documents and oaths over people.","internal_conflict":"She wonders whether her own secret shortcuts in the survey made the theft possible.","external_conflict":"Academy elders deny the loss to avoid scandal while the Cartel pressures the Wardens through tolls.","arc":"Orsolya leaves her archive, learns to act outside rules and records, and finds the courage to confess her mistake publicly.","personality_traits":["meticulous","gentle","anxious","principled"],"abilities":[{"name":"Skybridge Cartography","description":"Can reconstruct drift routes and weak points in the cloudstone network from fragments of survey data.","category":"mental"}]},{"id":"chr_dravik_solenne","name":"Dravik Solenne","description":"A silk-coated merchant prince of the Drift Cartel, rings on every finger and a perfumed smile that never reaches his eyes. He commissioned the theft of the map to control which bridges stay open and which tolls rise.","role":"antagonist","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":"fac_drift_cartel","motivation":"To make the Cartel the sole arbiter of safe passage, ensuring his house outlasts every rival.","goal":"Keep the map hidden and use its knowledge to force the Wardens and the Hollow Circle to accept higher tolls and levies.","flaw":"Arrogant belief that everything, and everyone, has a price.","internal_conflict":"He privately fears his charter-born power is hollow and one honest act could unravel it.","external_conflict":"The Toll War and Grain Levy have bred open resistance, and Kestrel's pursuit threatens to expose him.","arc":"Dravik tightens his grip, overreaches by leveraging wind-debts against his own allies, and loses his standing when the map is exposed.","personality_traits":["charming","calculating","vain","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Debt Leverage","description":"Weaponises wind-debt records to bind captains, officials and rivals to his will.","category":"social"}]},{"id":"chr_tamsin_rook","name":"Tamsin Rook","description":"A teenage deckhand and pickpocket raised on the quays of Mistral Docks, quick-fingered, freckled and always hungry. She was Kestrel's last recruit before the crew disbanded and knows the thief's habits better than she admits.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_mistral_docks","faction_id":null,"motivation":"To escape the dock gutters and win a berth on a ship of her own.","goal":"Earn enough from the map's recovery to pay off her family's wind-debt.","flaw":"Impulsive thieving that sabotages the trust she needs.","internal_conflict":"She idolises Kestrel's pirate past but is learning it left real victims.","external_conflict":"Cartel enforcers hunt her for a theft she once committed on Dravik's warehouse.","arc":"Tamsin trades petty theft for loyalty, using her skills to protect the crew and choosing a lawful path to her own ship.","personality_traits":["cheeky","fast-talking","loyal","hungry"],"abilities":[{"name":"Light Fingers","description":"Lifts keys, purses and papers unnoticed in crowded markets.","category":"physical"}]},{"id":"chr_bram_ashdown","name":"Bram Ashdown","description":"A broad-shouldered Bridge Warden engineer at Emberroost, soot-darkened and slow to speak, who braids cloudstone cables with enormous patience. He knows the map's missing sections would reveal which of his bridges the Cartel plans to let fail.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_emberroost","faction_id":"fac_bridge_wardens","motivation":"To keep every skybridge standing so no more crossings end in the sky.","goal":"Escort the recovered map to the Warden council and reinforce the weakest bridges before the season turns.","flaw":"Distrust of outsiders, especially pirates, which makes him rigid and unforgiving.","internal_conflict":"His oath to the Wardens clashes with his sense that the Wardens' bureaucracy has failed.","external_conflict":"Rising Cartel tolls starve his forge of funds, while Dravik's agents sabotage his shipments.","arc":"Bram sets aside prejudice, forms a hard-won bond with Kestrel, and breaks Warden protocol to save a bridge.","personality_traits":["stoic","loyal","stubborn","careful"],"abilities":[{"name":"Cloudstone Braiding","description":"Reads stress in cloudstone cable and can repair or sever a bridge with minimal tools.","category":"technological"}]},{"id":"chr_ilse_marrow","name":"Ilse Marrow","description":"A leader among the Hollow Circle millers, round-faced and sharp-eyed, who keeps a ledger of every Cartel levy. She offers shelter and intelligence to Kestrel in exchange for a promise to bring the Cartel's secrets to light.","role":"supporting","home_location_id":"loc_the_hollow","faction_id":"fac_hollow_circle","motivation":"To free her people from the Grain Levy that is draining their harvests.","goal":"Use the recovered map to prove Cartel manipulation and end the levy.","flaw":"Her fierce thrift makes her withhold aid until she is sure of repayment.","internal_conflict":"She feels guilty for once paying the levy quietly to protect her village.","external_conflict":"Cartel collectors threaten to seize the windmills if she resists.","arc":"Ilse turns from cautious bargaining to open defiance, rallying the isle to stand with Kestrel.","personality_traits":["shrewd","warm","tough","patient"],"abilities":[{"name":"Ledger Memory","description":"Recalls every levy, debt and shipment and spots forged accounts.","category":"mental"}]}],"relationships":[{"id":"rel_kestrel_dravik","source_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","target_character_id":"chr_dravik_solenne","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Kestrel Vane raided Dravik Solenne's cargo lanes for years, and he now holds her wind-debts over her while hiding the stolen map she hunts."},{"id":"rel_dravik_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_dravik_solenne","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Dravik Solenne sees Kestrel Vane as a debtor to be crushed and a threat to the map's secrecy, and sends enforcers after her."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orsolya Thane hires Kestrel Vane to recover the map, trusting a reformed pirate where the Academy and Wardens cannot act."},{"id":"rel_tamsin_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_tamsin_rook","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"mentor","description":"Tamsin Rook looks up to Kestrel Vane as a mentor, though she is torn between copying her piracy and following her new path."},{"id":"rel_bram_kestrel","source_character_id":"chr_bram_ashdown","target_character_id":"chr_kestrel_vane","relationship_type":"rival","description":"Bram Ashdown distrusts Kestrel Vane for her pirate past and challenges her at every step, until shared danger forges respect."},{"id":"rel_ilse_dravik","source_character_id":"chr_ilse_marrow","target_character_id":"chr_dravik_solenne","relationship_type":"enemy","description":"Ilse Marrow opposes Dravik Solenne's Grain Levy and seeks the map to expose his manipulation of the Hollow Circle."},{"id":"rel_orsolya_bram","source_character_id":"chr_orsolya_thane","target_character_id":"chr_bram_ashdown","relationship_type":"ally","description":"Orsolya Thane and Bram Ashdown are fellow Bridge Wardens who rely on each other to turn the recovered map into real bridge repairs."}]}
</Output>
